(The "for" loop allows us to repeat certain commands. If you want to repe\at )Tj
T*
(some action in a predetermined way, you can use the "for" loop. All of t\he loop )Tj
T*
(structures in matlab are started with a keyword such as "for", or "while\" and )Tj
T*
(they all end with the word "end". Another deep thought, eh. )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
(The "for" loop will loop around some statement, and you must tell Matlab\ )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(where to start and where to end. Basically, you give a vector in the "fo\r" )Tj
T*
(statement, and Matlab will loop through for each value in the vector: )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
(For example, a simple loop will go around four times: )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> for j=1:4,)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
