(a matrix. If you want to start at the second row of a matrix and subtrac\t the )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(previous row of the matrix and then repeat this operation on the followi\ng rows, )Tj
T*
(a "for" loop can do this in short order: )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> A = [ [1 2 3]' [3 2 1]' [2 1 3]'])Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(A =)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(     1     3     2)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(     2     2     1)Tj
T*
(     3     1     3)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(>> B = A;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> for j=2:3,)Tj
T*
(    A\(j,:\) = A\(j,:\) - A\(j-1,:\))Tj
T*
(end)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(A =)Tj
T*
(     1     3     2)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(     1    -1    -1)Tj
T*
