0 -6.15231 TD
(Another example where loops come in handy is the approximation of )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(differential equations. The following example approximates the D.E. y'=x\^2-)Tj
T*
(y^2, y\(0\)=1, using Euler's Method. First, the step size, h, is defined\. Once done, )Tj
T*
(the grid points are found, and an approximation is found. The approximat\ion is )Tj
T*
(simply a vector, y, in which the entry y\(j\) is the approximation at x\(\j\). )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> h = 0.1;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> x = [0:h:2];)Tj
T*
(>> y = 0*x;)Tj
T*
(>> y\(1\) = 1;)Tj
T*
(>> size\(x\))Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(ans =)Tj
T*
(     1    21)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(>> for i=2:21,)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    y\(i\) = y\(i-1\) + h*\(x\(i-1\)^2 - y\(i-1\)^2\);)Tj
T*
(   end)Tj
T*
(>> plot\(x,y\))Tj
T*
(>> plot\(x,y,'go'\))Tj
T*
(>> plot\(x,y,'go',x,y\))Tj
