13.77623 0 0 13.77623 151.87404 734.30048 Tm
(If you don't like the "for" loop, you can also use a "while" loop. The "\while" )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(loop repeats a sequence of commands as long as some condition is met. In\ this )Tj
T*
(example the D.E. y'=x-|y|, y\(0\)=1, is approximated using Euler's Metho\d: )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -3.76196 TD
(>> h = 0.001;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> x = [0:h:2];)Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
(>> y = 0*x;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> y\(1\) = 1;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> i = 1;)Tj
T*
(>> size\(x\))Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(ans =)Tj
T*
(           1        2001)Tj
T*
(>> max\(size\(x\)\))Tj
T*
(ans =)Tj
T*
(        2001)Tj
T*
(>> while\(i<max\(size\(x\)\)\))Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(     y\(i+1\) = y\(i\) + h*\(x\(i\)-abs\(y\(i\)\)\);)Tj
T*
(     i = i + 1;                         )Tj
T*
(   end)Tj
T*
(>> plot\(x,y,'go'\))Tj
T*
(>> plot\(x,y\))Tj
